    "done_when": "Repair the two code regressions the wave integration measurement attributed to this sprint's landings (report /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs/r-20261006T001835698222-cfs-wave-integration-suite/report.md, comparison module-comparison.json). (1) tests/test_biot_import_without_jax.py::test_grid_import_falls_back_to_host_without_jax fails at head because nova/biot/rangefunction.py now imports jax eagerly at module level (line 56, from the kernel compile-cost landing); make that import lazy or guarded so nova.biot imports and the host operator is used when jax is absent, exactly as the base did, without changing any traced arithmetic. (2) tests/test_route_solve_requests.py::test_exact_bank_replay_request_names_every_policy_deviation fails with TypeError: topology must be a TopologyPolicy, because the test rebuilds ForwardSolvePolicy from its to_dict() output and the topology field arrives as a mapping; ForwardSolvePolicy accepts a mapping for topology by converting it to TopologyPolicy in its own construction (the same conversion from_dict already performs), so a dict round trip reproduces an equal policy, and the TypeError stays for any other type. Done when both named tests pass at head, the two modules tests/test_biot_import_without_jax.py and tests/test_route_solve_requests.py pass in full, tests/test_forward_solve_request.py and tests/biot/test_kernel_compile_cost.py are unchanged in outcome against the base of this run, and a negative control shows the round trip refusing a non-mapping, non-policy topology value with the same TypeError. No test file is edited. Every check runs on compute or in place on the existing fleet allocation when the shell has SLURM_JOB_ID set, never as a heavy job on the login node; a single test module that finishes in seconds may run on the login node with JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv PYTHONPATH set to the run worktree (orientation_worktree in the manifest) uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider. Run each test module in its own fresh process, capture each run to one log under the run directory, and name every log in the manifest. Every uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. Judge by delta against the base revision (orientation_base_sha) for the same modules, and record baseline_suite and after_suite with module-qualified failure ids. Commit with conventional subjects and bodies; the manifest commits line lists every commit.",
